BT /F2 17 Tf 56 736 Td (Understanding the lights) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 702 Td 15 TL
(The front of the router has four lights. Power: solid green means the router is ready;) Tj T*
(blinking amber means it is starting up; solid red means a fault \(see Error codes on page 5\).) Tj T*
T*
(Internet: solid white means the router can reach the internet; blinking white means it is) Tj T*
(looking for a connection; off means the yellow WAN cable is not detected.) Tj T*
T*
(Wi-Fi: solid blue means both the 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz networks are on; blinking blue means a) Tj T*
(device is pairing with WPS; off means Wi-Fi has been switched off in the app.) Tj T*
T*
(Guest: solid green means the guest network is on. Guests can use the internet but cannot see) Tj T*
(your other devices or files.) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56 40 Td (Acme AirLink X200 Wi-Fi Router: User Guide \(sample document\)  -  Page 2 of 6) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
