BT /F2 17 Tf 56 736 Td (Troubleshooting and error codes) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 702 Td 15 TL
(No internet. Check that the yellow cable is firmly connected to the WAN port and to your) Tj T*
(modem. Restart the modem first, wait two minutes, then restart the router.) Tj T*
T*
(Slow Wi-Fi. Move closer to the router, keep it off the floor, and avoid placing it near) Tj T*
(metal objects. Devices that support 5 GHz will be faster at short range.) Tj T*
T*
(Error codes are shown in the AirLink app. E-12 means no WAN cable was detected. E-31 means) Tj T*
(the router's address conflicts with another device; restart your modem to fix it. E-47 means) Tj T*
(the router has overheated: unplug it, move it somewhere cooler with space around it, and) Tj T*
(wait 15 minutes before plugging it in. E-52 means the firmware is damaged: do a factory) Tj T*
(reset and then update the firmware.) Tj T*
T*
(If an error comes back after these steps, contact Acme Support with your serial number,) Tj T*
(which is printed on the label under the router.) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56 40 Td (Acme AirLink X200 Wi-Fi Router: User Guide \(sample document\)  -  Page 5 of 6) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
